.TH SDL_strnlen 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_strnlen \- This works exactly like strnlen() but doesn\(aqt require access to a C runtime.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_strnlen(const char *str, size_t maxlen);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Counts up to a maximum of
.BR maxlen
bytes in
.BR str ,
excluding the null terminator\[char46]
.PP
If you need the length of a UTF-8 string, consider using
.BR SDL_utf8strnlen ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I str
The null-terminated string to read\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I maxlen
The maximum amount of bytes to count\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the length (in bytes, excluding the null terminator) of
.BR src
but never more than
.BR maxlen \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_strlen (3),
.BR SDL_utf8strlen (3),
.BR SDL_utf8strnlen (3)
